Z||000000||Rodney||08-19-2001||08:22 AM||||There is a kit car mailing list but few post to it.<BR>Maybe we can get some of the kit car owners on the list<BR>and get some action going?<P>Thanks,<BR>Rodney Dickman<BR>New web page! <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P><BR>---------------------------------------------<P><BR>The KitCar List has been migrated to a new listserver.<P>Instructions/Information follows.<P><BR>To post to this list, send your email to:<P>  kitcar@alist4u.com<P>General information about the mailing list is at:<P>  <A HREF="http://alist4u.com/mailman/listinfo/kitcar" TARGET=_blank>http://alist4u.com/mailman/listinfo/kitcar</A> <P>If you ever want to unsubscribe or change your options<BR>(eg, switch to<BR>or from digest mode, change your password, etc.), visit<BR>your<BR>subscription page at:<P> <A HREF="http://alist4u.com/mailman/options/kitcar/rodney1%40exe" TARGET=_blank>http://alist4u.com/mailman/options/kitcar/rodney1%40exe</A> <BR>cpc.com<P>You can also make such adjustments via email by sending<BR>a message to:<P>  Kitcar-request@alist4u.com<P>with the word `help' in the subject or body (don't<BR>include the<BR>quotes), and you will get back a message with<BR>instructions.<P><BR>||||reg||1
